{
  "_comment": [
    "Go-vs-Python parity for 'which conf.d file declares which tenant' (#1942 blind review F1).",
    "Each tree is a conf.d built in a temp dir by BOTH sides. Go asserts pkg/config ScanDirTree",
    "(the exporter's walker: full ParseConfigFile decode, first YAML document only); Python asserts",
    "init_project._plan_confd. Neither reads the other's source; both assert this table.",
    "declarations: conf.d-relative path -> tenant ids, for every tenant file the exporter ACCEPTS",
    "  (a file it accepts that declares nothing is listed with []).",
    "rejected: tenant files the exporter's decode rejects (they declare nothing on any plane).",
    "conflict: the tenant id ScanDirTree reports as a cross-file duplicate, or null.",
    "init_unsure: files where init may answer 'cannot tell' instead of matching the exporter.",
    "  init then refuses (fail-closed) if the file names a requested tenant; Go ignores the field.",
    "Files starting with '_' and anything under a dot-directory are in neither list: the exporter",
    "never reads them as tenant files."
  ],
